    "id": "kmp-compose-multiplatform-ui",
    "title": "🎨 Compose Multiplatform UI Engine & Atomic Design System",
    "domain": "3. UI & Design System",
    "description": "Master-tier guide for building high-performance, warning-free UI components in Compose Multiplatform (CMP) across Android, iOS, Desktop (JVM / Skiko), and Web (Wasm / JS). Covers Atomic Design System modeling, Coil 3.x async image pipelines, Slot API architecture, Retina/HiDPI scaling, and Skiko rendering optimizations. Use this skill whenever: 1. Designing reusable UI component kits (Buttons, Cards, Inputs, Modals, TopBars) in Compose Multiplatform. 2. Integrating Coil 3.x for cross-platform remote and cached image loading. 3. Resolving Skiko rendering glitches, font blurry artifacts, or HiDPI scaling across Desktop and Web. 4. Structuring Composable functions with slot APIs, state hoisting, and standard Modifier conventions. 5. Building accessible, touch-friendly, and responsive design systems on KMP. Do NOT use when: 1. Managing application navigation stacks (use `kmp-navigation-compose-stack`). 2. Designing raw multi-palette token engines (use `kmp-design-tokens-theme-engine`).",
